 "drivingQuestion": "What is the state of מתנמנם?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Rav Ashi defines the term",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "megillah.18b.9",
   "daf": "18b",
   "sentenceId": 8,
   "he": "מִתְנַמְנֵם יָצָא וְכוּ׳. הֵיכִי דָּמֵי מִתְנַמְנֵם? אָמַר רַב אָשֵׁי: נִים וְלָא נִים, תִּיר וְלָא תִּיר, דְּקָרוּ לֵיהּ וְעָנֵי וְלָא יָדַע לְאַהְדּוֹרֵי סְבָרָא, וְכִי מַדְכְּרוּ לֵיהּ מִידְּכַר.",
   "en": "§ It is taught in the mishna: If one read the Megilla «while he is dozing off, he has fulfilled his» obligation. The Gemara asks: «What are the circumstances of» the case of «dozing off? Rav Ashi said:» It is referring to a situation in which one is «asleep yet not» fully «asleep, awake yet not» fully «awake. If someone calls him he answers. And he is» in a mental state in which «he does not know» how «to provide» an answer that requires logical «reasoning, but when people remind him» about something that has happened, «he remembers» it."
  }
